---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BriefingForm from '../../components/BriefingForm.astro';
import CallToAction from '../../components/CallToAction.astro';
import 'katex/dist/katex.min.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="Solutions - Deterministic Security & Verifiable Compliance - Decoheron">
    <div class="container py-4">
        <!-- Hero Section -->
        <div class="row mb-5">
            <div class="col-lg-9">
                <span class="badge bg-primary mb-3 px-3 py-2 text-uppercase fs-6">
                    Managed Security & Compliance
                </span>
                <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold text-primary mb-3">
                    Deterministic Controls.<br>Verifiable Proof.
                </h1>
                <p class="lead text-subtle fs-5">
                    Every control we deploy is built to satisfy three separate audiences at once: your insurer, your regulator, and a court asking whether the board exercised reasonable care, if it ever comes to that. We don't attest to security. We prove it, continuously, with a signed record.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Four Outcomes -->
        <div class="mb-5">
            <div class="mb-4">
                <h2 class="h3 fw-bold text-primary">Four Outcomes, One Deterministic Control Set</h2>
                <p class="text-secondary fw-medium">Every engagement is scoped against these four liabilities, not just against threats</p>
            </div>
            <div class="row g-4">
                <!-- Insurance-Grade Protection -->
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card bg-light h-100 p-4 rounded-3 border border-2 border-secondary shadow-lg">
                        <span class="text-secondary fw-bold text-uppercase fs-6 mb-2">Company Risk</span>
                        <h3 class="h5 fw-bold text-primary mb-3">Insurance-Grade Protection</h3>
                        <p class="mb-0 text-body fs-6">
                            Insurers are increasingly voiding claims where attested controls, such as "organisation-wide MFA," cannot be independently verified at the time of loss. We build to the standard underwriters recognise and negotiate directly with them for improved terms, so your policy pays out when it matters.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <!-- Director Defensibility -->
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card bg-light h-100 p-4 rounded-3 border border-2 border-secondary shadow-lg">
                        <span class="text-secondary fw-bold text-uppercase fs-6 mb-2">Personal Risk</span>
                        <h3 class="h5 fw-bold text-primary mb-3">Director Defensibility</h3>
                        <p class="mb-0 text-body fs-6">
                            Section 180 exposure is personal, and it survives whatever coverage the company carries. We align your control environment to SMB1001 Level 3 (Gold) — and exceed it in the areas examined first under forensic review — so individual directors have an independently verifiable standard of care to point to.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <!-- Operational Continuity -->
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card bg-light h-100 p-4 rounded-3 border border-2 border-secondary shadow-lg">
                        <span class="text-secondary fw-bold text-uppercase fs-6 mb-2">Business Risk</span>
                        <h3 class="h5 fw-bold text-primary mb-3">Operational Continuity</h3>
                        <p class="mb-0 text-body fs-6">
                            Prevention will eventually fail once; containment cannot be allowed to fail alongside it. We architect around minimal blast radius, so a single compromised credential or device is a contained incident, not a firm-wide outage or a notifiable data breach.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <!-- Proof of Care -->
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card bg-light h-100 p-4 rounded-3 border border-2 border-secondary shadow-lg">
                        <span class="text-secondary fw-bold text-uppercase fs-6 mb-2">Evidentiary Risk</span>
                        <h3 class="h5 fw-bold text-primary mb-3">Proof of Care</h3>
                        <p class="mb-0 text-body fs-6">
                            A control that cannot be evidenced at a specific point in time is, forensically and legally, indistinguishable from a control that did not exist. We issue timestamped, cryptographically signed reports on control status, on a regular cadence — a contemporaneous record your insurer, regulator, or counsel can rely on without taking your word for it.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- What This Looks Like In Practice -->
        <div class="row justify-content-center mb-5">
            <div class="col-lg-10">
                <div class="p-4 border-0">
                    <h2 class="h3 fw-bold text-primary mb-4 text-center">
                        What This Looks Like In Practice
                    </h2>
                    <div class="row g-4">
                        <!-- Item 1 -->
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="d-flex align-items-start gap-3">
                                <span class="square-bullet mt-1">■</span>
                                <div>
                                    <h3 class="h5 fw-bold text-primary">No Passwords Left to Steal</h3>
                                    <p class="text-body mb-0">
                                        Passwordless authentication and passkeys are enforced organisation-wide, removing the single most common vector in credential-based breaches — not offered as an opt-in for staff who choose to use it.
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Item 2 -->
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="d-flex align-items-start gap-3">
                                <span class="square-bullet mt-1">■</span>
                                <div>
                                    <h3 class="h5 fw-bold text-primary">Zero Standing Access</h3>
                                    <p class="text-body mb-0">
                                        No individual — including us — holds permanent administrative rights. Elevated access is granted just-in-time, scoped to the task, and automatically revoked and logged.
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Item 3 -->
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="d-flex align-items-start gap-3">
                                <span class="square-bullet mt-1">■</span>
                                <div>
                                    <h3 class="h5 fw-bold text-primary">Deterministic Access Policy</h3>
                                    <p class="text-body mb-0">
                                        Conditional Access policies deny any authentication attempt that does not meet policy, by default. This is not a monitored exception queue — non-compliant access is structurally impossible, not merely flagged.
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Item 4 -->
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="d-flex align-items-start gap-3">
                                <span class="square-bullet mt-1">■</span>
                                <div>
                                    <h3 class="h5 fw-bold text-primary">Application Control by Default</h3>
                                    <p class="text-body mb-0">
                                        Only explicitly approved software is permitted to execute. Ransomware payloads and unauthorised tooling are blocked at execution, rather than detected afterward by an analyst reviewing alerts.
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Item 5 -->
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="d-flex align-items-start gap-3">
                                <span class="square-bullet mt-1">■</span>
                                <div>
                                    <h3 class="h5 fw-bold text-primary">Immutable, Segmented Backups</h3>
                                    <p class="text-body mb-0">
                                        Backups are unreachable and unalterable from a compromised account, including a compromised administrator account, and systems are segmented so no single failure point can cascade firm-wide.
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Item 6 -->
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="d-flex align-items-start gap-3">
                                <span class="square-bullet mt-1">■</span>
                                <div>
                                    <h3 class="h5 fw-bold text-primary">Signed, Timestamped Reporting</h3>
                                    <p class="text-body mb-0">
                                        Control status is reported on a regular cadence and cryptographically signed at time of issue, producing a tamper-evident record rather than a retrospective, self-assessed attestation.
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Framework Alignment -->
        <div class="row g-4 mb-5">
            <div class="col-12">
                <h2 class="h3 fw-bold text-primary mb-1">
                    Framework Alignment
                </h2>
                <p class="text-secondary fw-medium mb-0">Deterministic controls, mapped against the standards insurers, regulators, and forensic examiners actually apply</p>
            </div>
            <!-- Essential Eight -->
            <div class="col-md-4">
                <div class="card bg-light h-100 border border-2 border-secondary shadow-lg p-4 rounded-3">
                    <div class="mb-3">
                        <h3 class="h4 fw-bold text-primary mb-1">Essential Eight</h3>
                        <p class="text-secondary mb-0 fw-medium">Insurer & Regulator Baseline</p>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-body mb-3">
                        We deploy to Maturity Level 1 as a floor, not a ceiling, because it remains the reference point underwriters and regulators default to when assessing whether reasonable controls were in place.
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-body mb-0">
                        With the ASD sunsetting Essential Eight, we've already transitioned our primary alignment forward — your organisation is positioned ahead of the standard's replacement, not scrambling to catch up to it.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <!-- SMB1001 -->
            <div class="col-md-4">
                <div class="card bg-light h-100 border border-2 border-secondary shadow-lg p-4 rounded-3">
                    <div class="mb-3">
                        <h3 class="h4 fw-bold text-primary mb-1">SMB1001 Level 3 (Gold)</h3>
                        <p class="text-secondary mb-0 fw-medium">Director-Grade Standard of Care</p>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-body mb-3">
                        Purpose-built for organisations of your size, SMB1001 Gold gives individual directors an independently published, third-party standard to point to — rather than an internal policy of the board's own making.
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-body mb-0">
                        We exceed Gold specifically in passkey enforcement, application control, and zero standing admin access — the control areas examined first in a post-incident forensic review.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <!-- Verifiable Compliance -->
            <div class="col-md-4">
                <div class="card h-100 bg-light border border-2 border-secondary shadow-lg p-4 rounded-3">
                    <div class="mb-3">
                        <h3 class="h4 fw-bold text-primary mb-1">Continuous Verification</h3>
                        <p class="text-secondary mb-0 fw-medium">Evidence, Not Attestation</p>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-body mb-3">
                        Framework alignment on paper is a starting position, not an outcome. Controls are technically enforced, not policy-only, and their operation is verified on an ongoing basis.
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-body mb-0">
                        The full ISM / Essential Eight / SMB1001 control mapping, with our specific implementation against each, is available for your broker, auditor, or counsel on request.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <CallToAction />
    </div>
    <BriefingForm hidden={true} />
</BaseLayout>
